  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "The current best (config_020: scvi_n200, vit_l, avgpool, concat, acc 0.715) establishes a strong baseline. The largest remaining uncertainty is the RNA encoder choice: we have only tested pca_n2000 and scvi_n200, while scgpt is completely unexplored. config_021 changes exactly one variable from config_020 (RNA encoder scvi_n200 → scgpt) while holding the known-best image encoder (vit_l), aggregation (avgpool), fusion (concat), and profile setting (multiprofile) fixed. This isolates the effect of the RNA representation. Because scgpt is a generative single-cell model with a fundamentally different inductive bias than scvi, the prior uncertainty is high—it could substantially outperform or underperform scvi_n200. By contrast, the aggregation question (avgpool vs transformer) already has evidence favoring avgpool (config_003 vs config_014, ~4-pt gap), making a transformer test with vit_l lower expected information gain. Testing scgpt is therefore the highest-value single-variable experiment: it either confirms scvi_n200 as the preferred RNA encoder or reveals a new promising direction, directly reducing uncertainty about a core design axis under the limited budget."
}

